**Given:**

The first number = 0.08

The second number = 0.32

**Formula Used:**

Mean Proportional =sqrt{{First number} times {Second number}}

**Calculation:**

Mean Proportional = sqrt{0.08 times 0.32}

Mean Proportional = sqrt{0.0256}

Mean Proportional = 0.16

**The mean proportional between 0.08 and 0.32 is 0.16.**
